    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The cell is the fundamental structural and functional unit of all living organisms.",
        "Robert Hooke discovered cells in 1665, while Anton von Leeuwenhoek first observed live cells.",
        "Schleiden, Schwann, and Virchow formulated the Cell Theory stating all organisms consist of cells arising from pre-existing cells.",
        "Prokaryotic cells lack membrane-bound nuclei and organelles, whereas eukaryotic cells possess a compartmentalized structure.",
        "Mitochondria generate cellular energy in the form of ATP, while lysosomes contain hydrolytic enzymes for cellular digestion."
      ],
      "id": "mmqkits"
    },
