    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Rudolf Virchow contributed the phrase 'Omnis cellula-e cellula' indicating all cells arise from pre-existing cells.",
        "Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semi-autonomous organelles possessing their own circular DNA and 70S ribosomes.",
        "Lysosomes are frequently asked in exams as 'suicidal bags' due to their acid hydrolases.",
        "Ribosomes are unique non-membrane-bound organelles present in both prokaryotic and eukaryotic organisms."
      ],
      "id": "k30jhpi"
